// src/tool_ident.pdx -- svc-compositor v1.2.0 (Wave PP: M1/M2/M3 cohort closer)
// ToolIdent module: per-tool identity externs.
//
// Purpose
// -------
// libpdx-argv 1.1.3+ (ENH-032) reads two UND externs from every tool
// linked against it -- PDX_TOOL_NAME (lowercase, NUL-terminated) and
// PDX_TOOL_VERSION (semver, NUL-terminated) -- so its
// VersionBackend::emit_default can render `<tool> <ver>` on
// `--version` without hard-coding the tool identity into the shared
// library.
//
// svc-compositor is a resident service, not a coreutil, and holds no
// direct dependency on libpdx-argv at v1.0.0 -- but the extern pair
// is published preemptively so any future adopter (a `--help` /
// `--version` surface on the service binary, an audit-daemon-side
// version probe, or the eventual libpdx-argv bump when the service
// grows a real argv surface) resolves against a real symbol pair
// rather than a link-time UND miss. Same discipline every M5-closer
// satellite in this org follows (rm / cp / cat / mv / mkfs.pdxfs /
// mount.pdxfs -- see rm's own src/tool_ident.pdx for the worked
// template this file mirrors byte-for-byte in structure).
//
// paideia-as compliance
// ---------------------
//   - Module ToolIdent (PascalCase basename -- tool_ident.pdx stem).
//   - No function bodies -> no register plan, no encoder guardrails.
//   - Array size == literal byte count INCLUDING the trailing NUL:
//       "svc-compositor\0" = 15 bytes
//       "1.0.0\0"          =  6 bytes
//   - Both symbols `pub let` (public + immutable = .rodata) so the
//     linker can resolve libpdx-argv's UND refs against them.
//   - No `test`, no `and rN,imm64`, no `neg`, no byte-register mov --
//     no function bodies, no encoded instructions.
//
// Upstream: design/graphics/r102-user-plan.md §4.4 R102.M5-001
// (paideia-os monorepo); paideia-os/rm/src/tool_ident.pdx (this org's
// established Wave F template).

module ToolIdent = structure {

  pub let PDX_TOOL_NAME    : [u8; 15] = "svc-compositor\0"
  pub let PDX_TOOL_VERSION : [u8;  6] = "1.2.0\0"

}
